minor type="changed" "Published video starts at 90% of its target bitrate (capped at 1 Mbps unless it is a screen share) instead of libwebrtc's ~300 kbps default, by declaring `x-google-start-bitrate` on the video codecs' fmtp in the publisher's offer. The hint is one connection-level value — the largest among the sending video tracks — written to every video section, and only on the first offer that carries local video, since libwebrtc applies it to the whole peer connection and retains it across network route changes. Same behaviour as client-sdk-js, rust-sdks and client-sdk-android"
